          %p
            More details for the moment at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Weil+theory+introduction"} ∞-Chern-Weil theory introduction
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+algebra+cocycle"} ∞-Lie algebra cocycle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} Chern-Simons element
            %li
              %p
                %strong> invariant polynomial
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+theory"} invariant theory
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The idea of invariant polynomials as a
            = succeed "-invariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory"} Chern-Weil theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Weil"}> André Weil
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Géométrie différentielle des espaces fibres
                = succeed "," do
                  %em André Weil Oeuvres Scientifiques / Collected Papers
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9783662452561"} ISBN:978-3-662-45256-1
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Cartan"}> Henri Cartan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cohomologie réelle d’un espace fibré principal différentiable. I : notions d’algèbre différentielle, algèbre de Weil d’un groupe de Lie
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=SHC_1949-1950__2__A18_0"} numdam:SHC_1949-1950__2__A18_0
              %p
                %br/
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Cartan"}> Henri Cartan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notions d’algèbre différentielle; applications aux groupes de Lie et aux variétés où opère un groupe de Lie
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Colloque de Topologie (Espaces Fibrés) Tenu à Bruxelles du 5 au 8 juin 1950
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://books.google.de/books/about/Colloque_de_topologie_espaces_fibres.html?id=sagqHQAACAAJ&redir_esc=y"} GoogleBooks
              %p
                %br/
              %p (These two articles have the same content, with the same section outline, but not the same wording. The first one is a tad more detailed.)
            %li#Chern50
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shiing-shen+Chern"}> Shiing-shen Chern
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential geometry of fiber bundles
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Chern-DifferentialGeometryOfFiberBundles.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mathunion.org/fileadmin/ICM/Proceedings/ICM1950.2/ICM1950.2.ocr.pdf"} full proceedings vol 2 pdf
            %li#KobayashiNomizu63
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shoshichi+Kobayashi"}> Shoshichi Kobayashi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Katsumi+Nomizu"} Katsumi Nomizu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Foundations of Differential Geometry, Volume 1
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.zuj.edu.jo/download/foundations-of-differential-geometry-vol-1-kobayashi-nomizu-pdf/"} web
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.wiley.com/en-us/Foundations+of+Differential+Geometry%2C+Volume+1-p-9780471157335"} ISBN:9780471157335
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foundations_of_Differential_Geometry"} Wikipedia
          %p
            Invariant polynomials for Lie algebras of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+Lie+groups"} simple Lie groups
            are disussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"}> José de Azcárraga
              , A. J. Macfarlane, A. J. Mountain, J. C. Perez Bueno,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Invariant tensors for simple groups
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/physics/9706006"} arXiv:physics/9706006
          %p A standard textbook account of the traditional theory is in volume III of
          %ul
            %li#GHV
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Werner+Greub"}> Werner Greub
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Halperin"} Stephen Halperin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ray+Vanstone"} Ray Vanstone
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Connections%2C+Curvature%2C+and+Cohomology"} Connections, Curvature, and Cohomology
              Academic Press (1973)
          %p
            The notion of invariant polynomials of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-connections
              (
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos+--+references#SSSI"}> web
              ).
          %p
            Discussion via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
          %ul
            %li#FreedHopkins13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                %em
                  %em> Chern-Weil forms and abstract homotopy theory
                  , Bull. Amer. Math. Soc.
                  %strong 50
                  (2013) 431-468 &amp;lbrack;
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.5959"}> arXiv:1301.5959
                  ,
                  = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/bull/2013-50-03/S0273-0979-2013-01415-0"} doi:S0273-0979-2013-01415-0
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (via
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Grady"}> Daniel Grady
                \:
                %em On the differential K-theory of moduli stacks
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.03108"}> arXiv:2501.03108
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (via
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
                  and
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
          %p
            An account in the more general context of Lie theory in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes"} cohesive (infinity,1)-toposes
            is in section 3.3.11 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
              \.
